  "worked_solution": "The notation $a∤b$ means $a$ does not divides $b.$ So, $3∤5$ means $3\\text{ doesn't divide }5.$\n\nAccording to the definition of integer divisibility, the fact that $a$ does not divide $b$ means that for any integer $k,$ we have that \n\n$$\nb\\ne ak.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, $3∤5$ is equivalent to the statement that $\\text{for any}$ $\\text{integer}$ $k,$ we have $5\\ne 3k.$",
